  "text": "Vanishing made the Mona Lisa famous. On Monday, 21 August 1911, a glazier who once worked there carried it out through a service door. Nobody noticed for a whole day. Then the papers went wild, and the Louvre shut for a week. When it reopened, crowds queued to stare at the empty wall where it hung. Police even questioned Pablo Picasso. Meanwhile, it sat in a trunk in the thief's Paris room for over two years. In December 1913, he tried to sell it to a dealer in Florence, and was caught. Turns out, the theft helped make her the most famous painting on Earth.",
