 "caption": "Did you know the Mona Lisa was once stolen? 🖼️\n\nOn Monday 21 August 1911, Vincenzo Peruggia, a glazier who had briefly worked at the Louvre, lifted the Mona Lisa off its four iron pegs and carried it out through a service door. Nobody noticed for about a day. The papers went wild, the Louvre closed for a week, and when it reopened crowds queued just to stare at the empty wall. Police even questioned Pablo Picasso. For two years the painting sat in a trunk in Peruggia's Paris room, until December 1913, when he tried to sell it to an art dealer in Florence and was caught. The theft helped turn it into the most famous painting on Earth.\n\nSend this to the friend who has queued to see her.\n\nImages: Library of Congress and Wikimedia Commons (public domain).",
